You may see: E: Package 'azure-cli' has no installation candidate if the Microsoft apt repository was not added correctly.
Inspect the repo file: cat /etc/apt/sources.list.d/azure-cli.list â it must contain a single unbroken deb line; if the file is empty or malformed, delete it and re-run the install script.
Official guide: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli-linux
# 5. Google Cloud CLI
sudo apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates

curl -fsSL https://packages.cloud.google.com/apt/doc/apt-key.gpg \
  | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/cloud.google.gpg

printf 'deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/cloud.google.gpg] https://packages.cloud.google.com/apt cloud-sdk main\n' \
